      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the remainder when the sum of the first five prime numbers is divided by the sixth prime number. Let's proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, identify the first six prime numbers:\n\\[2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13\\]\n\nNext, calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers:\n\\[2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\\]\n\nPerform the addition step by step:\n\\[2 + 3 = 5\\]\n\\[5 + 5 = 10\\]\n\\[10 + 7 = 17\\]\n\\[17 + 11 = 28\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five prime numbers is:\n\\[28\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by the sixth prime number, which is 13. This can be done using the modulo operation:\n\\[28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\nThis means:\n\\[28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2\\]\nThe remainder is 2.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is:\n\\[\\boxed{2}\\]",
