    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The steps to solve the problem are as follows:\n\n1. **Find the first six prime numbers**: \n   - The first prime number is \\(2\\).\n   - The second prime number is \\(3\\).\n   - The third prime number is \\(5\\).\n   - The fourth prime number is \\(7\\).\n   - The fifth prime number is \\(11\\).\n   - The sixth prime number is \\(13\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers**: \n   \\[\n   2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n   \\]\n   Let's add these step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 + 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   10 + 7 = 17\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   17 + 11 = 28\n   \\]\n   So, the sum of the first five prime numbers is \\(28\\).\n\n3. **Find the remainder when the sum is divided by the sixth prime number**: \n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum of the first five primes} = 28\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sixth prime number} = 13\n   \\]\n   We need to find \\(28 \\mod 13\\).\n\n4. **Calculate the remainder**:\n   \\[\n   28 \\div 13\n   \\]\n   Performing the division:\n   \\[\n   28 \\div 13 = 2 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 28 - (13 \\times 2) = 28 - 26 = 2\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the remainder when \\(28\\) is divided by \\(13\\) is \\(2\\).\n\nThe final answer, boxed, is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
